Below is a **production-style image upload + retrieve setup** using Laravel’s **Storage facade** for your Real Estate project (Property images). This works cleanly with Blade and avoids common “image not showing” issues.

---

## 1) One-time setup (MOST IMPORTANT)

### ✅ Set disk to public + create symlink

Run:

```bash
php artisan storage:link
```

This creates:
`public/storage  -> storage/app/public`

### ✅ .env (usually default)

```env
FILESYSTEM_DISK=public
```

---

## 2) Store single “main image” for Property

### ✅ Controller (store)

```php
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Storage;

public function store(Request $request)
{
    $request->validate([
        'title' => 'required|string|max:150',
        'price' => 'required|numeric|min:0',
        'image' => 'nullable|image|mimes:jpg,jpeg,png,webp|max:2048',
    ]);

    $data = $request->only(['title','price','description','category_id','city','address']);
    $data['agent_id'] = auth()->id();

    // Upload image
    if ($request->hasFile('image')) {
        $data['image'] = $request->file('image')->store('properties', 'public');
        // example stored path: properties/abc123.webp
    }

    $property = Property::create($data);

    return redirect()->route('agent.properties.show', $property->id)
        ->with('success', 'Property created.');
}
```

### ✅ Controller (update + delete old image)

```php
public function update(Request $request, Property $property)
{
    abort_if($property->agent_id !== auth()->id(), 403);

    $request->validate([
        'title' => 'required|string|max:150',
        'price' => 'required|numeric|min:0',
        'image' => 'nullable|image|mimes:jpg,jpeg,png,webp|max:2048',
    ]);

    $data = $request->only(['title','price','description','category_id','city','address']);

    if ($request->hasFile('image')) {
        // delete old
        if ($property->image && Storage::disk('public')->exists($property->image)) {
            Storage::disk('public')->delete($property->image);
        }

        // store new
        $data['image'] = $request->file('image')->store('properties', 'public');
    }

    $property->update($data);

    return back()->with('success', 'Property updated.');
}
```

### ✅ Delete property (delete image too)

```php
public function destroy(Property $property)
{
    abort_if($property->agent_id !== auth()->id(), 403);

    if ($property->image && Storage::disk('public')->exists($property->image)) {
        Storage::disk('public')->delete($property->image);
    }

    $property->delete();

    return redirect()->route('agent.properties.index')->with('success', 'Deleted.');
}
```

